# Environment variables for this lab.
#
# Nothing loads this file. Export a variable in your shell, or put it in front of
# one command:  GHCP_MODEL=gemini-4-neon claude-gemini
# Every line is commented out, so sourcing the file as it is changes nothing.
# Command-line options (--ghcp-model, --bridge-port) win over these variables.

# --- Launcher (bin/claude-gemini) ---------------------------------------------

# Gemini 4 model Claude Code starts on. --ghcp-model overrides it.
# One of: gemini-4-argon, gemini-4-carbon, gemini-4-hydrogen, gemini-4-neon.
# Default: gemini-4-hydrogen.
# GHCP_MODEL=gemini-4-hydrogen

# Fixed loopback port for the bridge. Same as --bridge-port (1 to 65535).
# Default: none, a free port is chosen.
# GHCP_BRIDGE_PORT=4142

# 1 turns on Claude Code's native MCP tool search; 0 keeps it off.
# Default: 0.
# GHCP_NATIVE_TOOL_SEARCH=0

# Directory of the persistent bridge (used by every launch except -p): its
# registry, lock, bridge.log and per-launch settings. Use an absolute path.
# Default: ~/Library/Caches/<package name> on macOS,
#          ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/<package name> elsewhere,
#          where <package name> is the "name" in package.json.
# GHCP_DAEMON_DIR=/absolute/path/to/bridge-directory

# The real Claude Code executable the launcher runs.
# Default: the first `claude` on PATH that is not one of this repository's launchers.
# CLAUDE_CODE_BIN=/absolute/path/to/claude

# Claude Code's fullscreen renderer. The launcher sets 1 when this is unset.
# CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1

# --- LiteLLM path (bin/claude-gemini-litellm, bin/gemini-litellm) ---------------
# See guide-litellm.html. --litellm-model and --litellm-base-url win over these.

# LiteLLM model alias Claude Code starts on.
# One of: gemini-4-argon, gemini-4-carbon, gemini-4-hydrogen, gemini-4-neon.
# Default: gemini-4-hydrogen.
# LITELLM_MODEL=gemini-4-neon

# LiteLLM root URL, without /v1. For a gateway other than this machine's, also set
# LITELLM_API_KEY.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:4000 (the port gemini-litellm up uses).
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# Port gemini-litellm up gives LiteLLM (1 to 65535), and the port claude-gemini-litellm
# connects to when LITELLM_BASE_URL is unset. --port overrides it for gemini-litellm up.
# Default: 4000.
# LITELLM_PORT=4000

# The key Claude Code sends to LiteLLM. Against this machine's gateway it is read
# from litellm-master-key in the LiteLLM home when unset, so you rarely set it.
# LITELLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# Where gemini-litellm installs LiteLLM and keeps its key, log, state, bridge
# directory and Claude Code settings files. Use an absolute path.
# Default: .runtime/ in this repository (git-ignored).
# GEMINI_LITELLM_HOME=/absolute/path/to/litellm-home

# --- Bridge (every bridge; changing one replaces the persistent bridge) --------

# Gemini 4 sometimes answers a model call with nothing at all. The Copilot runtime
# can retry such a call (its STREAM_INTERRUPTION_RECOVERY feature), and the bridge
# turns that on for the runtime it starts. 0 leaves the decision to the runtime.
# Default: on.
# GHCP_STREAM_RECOVERY=0

# Copilot configuration and login directory.
# Default: ~/.copilot
# COPILOT_HOME=/absolute/path/to/.copilot

# A model with no progress for this long fails the turn (ms), and so does a turn
# that runs longer than the maximum (ms).
# Default: 300000 and 1800000.
# TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
# TURN_MAX_DURATION_MS=1800000

# Largest request body, and the most saved history replayed into a new session (bytes).
# Default: 268435456 (256 MiB) each.
# MAX_BODY_BYTES=268435456
# MAX_REPLAY_BYTES=268435456

# Copilot runtime log level.
# Default: error.
# LOG_LEVEL=error

# --- Worth knowing -------------------------------------------------------------

# COPILOT_CLI_PATH makes the bridge run that Copilot CLI instead of the runtime the
# SDK ships. A Copilot CLI session exports it, so run this lab from a fresh terminal
# or `unset COPILOT_CLI_PATH`. gemini-doctor warns when it is set. The CLI it names
# must speak SDK protocol 4; an older one stops the bridge with "SDK protocol
# version mismatch".
#
# COPILOT_SDK_DEFAULT_CONNECTION is the SDK's own transport selector. The bridge
# always starts the runtime as a child process, so it has no effect here; leave it
# unset.
